---
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro'
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site'
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use" description="Terms of use for the Dunder Mifflin placeholder-data API." active="docs">
  <Sidebar />

  <div class="stack">
    <Panel title="Terms of Use">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>By using the Dunder Mifflin API (the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;) you agree to these terms.</p>

        <h2>1. What you may do</h2>
        <p>
          Use the Service, free of charge, in personal, educational and commercial projects: prototypes, demos, tests,
          seed data, screenshots, teaching material. Attribution is appreciated but not required.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What you may not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Present the data as describing real people, or use it to deceive anyone.</li>
          <li>Send traffic that would be unreasonable for a free service, such as scraping in a tight loop or using the Service as a production CDN for images.</li>
          <li>Resell access to the Service or claim it as your own.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Fan project and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to
          NBCUniversal, Universal Television, Deedle-Dee Productions, or anyone involved in producing
          <em>The Office</em>. Character names and likenesses are the property of their respective owners and are used
          here for placeholder and parody purposes. All emails, phone numbers, addresses and biographies are fictional
          and were written for this Service.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you hold rights in any material served here and would like it removed, email
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Takedown%20request`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and it will be taken down
          promptly.
        </p>

        <h2>4. No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;, without warranty of any kind. It may change, go down, or go
          away. Do not build anything that people depend on directly against it; copy the data you need into your own
          project instead.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, the operator of the Service is not liable for any loss or damage
          arising from its use.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Changes</h2>
        <p>These terms may be updated from time to time. Continued use after a change means you accept it.</p>

        <p class="text-dm-muted">Last updated 22 September 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </Panel>
  </div>
</Layout>
